<!doctype html>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Ligos — Sauleis Bazdā &rarr; Mazdō-yō Heardō̃</title>
<style>
  @font-face { font-family:'Ligos'; src:url('/fonts/ligos-regular.woff2') format('woff2'); font-weight:400; font-style:normal; font-display:swap; }
  @font-face { font-family:'Ligos'; src:url('/fonts/ligos-bold.woff2') format('woff2'); font-weight:700; font-style:normal; font-display:swap; }
  @font-face { font-family:'Ligos'; src:url('/fonts/ligos-italic.woff2') format('woff2'); font-weight:400; font-style:italic; font-display:swap; }
  body { font-family:'Ligos', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; max-width: 42rem; margin: 3rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; line-height: 1.65; color: #1a1320; background: #fbf8f3; }
  h1, h2 { font-variant: small-caps; letter-spacing: .03em; color: #5a1530; }
  h1 { font-size: 2.6rem; margin-bottom: 0; }
  .sub { color: #8a6d3b; font-style: italic; margin-top: .2rem; }
  .heart { color: #8a1538; font-weight: bold; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 1rem 0; }
  td, th { border-bottom: 1px solid #e4dccc; padding: .35rem .7rem; text-align: left; }
  th { color: #5a1530; }
  code { background: #efe9dd; padding: 0 .3rem; border-radius: 3px; }
  .big { font-size: 1.5rem; }
  ul { line-height: 2; }
  footer { margin-top: 3rem; color: #998; font-size: .85rem; border-top: 1px solid #e4dccc; padding-top: 1rem; }
</style>

<h1>{{ Txt.cap(SCArs.evolve("ligā")) }}</h1>
<p class="sub">Sauleis Bazdā &rarr; Mazdō-yō Heardō̃ · the Solar Speech becomes the Heart Speech</p>

<p>This page is hosted by <b>Hymn</b>, the web server of the <b>Orpheus</b> environment.
Not one Heart Speech word below is written into the page — each is produced at request
time by calling <code>SCArs.evolve</code>, the sound-change applier, which derives the
modern <span class="heart">Heart Speech</span> form from its ancient Solar Speech
ancestor. The page is written in <em>Facet</em>, Orpheus' markup language.</p>

<h2>Core vocabulary</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Solar Speech</th><th>Heart Speech (via SCArs)</th></tr>
  {{each w in ["ligā", "dīwā", "bazdā", "Naktā", "orpā", "asā", "apā", "moisā", "kósmā", "sālā", "wōkā", "zāwā", "weidā", "zelā", "serdā", "sanā", "dázā", "zerā", "menā", "berzā"]}}
  <tr><td><code>{{w}}</code></td><td class="heart">{{ SCArs.evolve(w) }}</td></tr>
  {{end}}
</table>

<h2>Nasal vowels &amp; the bundled font</h2>
<p>Heart Speech nasalizes vowels before lost coda nasals. When a <em>long</em> vowel
nasalizes, the result stacks a macron and a tilde over a single vowel — e.g.
<span class="heart big">{{ SCArs.evolve("nūn") }}</span>. These render correctly because
Hymn serves the bundled <i>Ligos</i> Unicode font (with mark-positioning) over
<code>@font-face</code>; every word here is, again, generated by SCArs:</p>
<ul>
  <li><span class="heart big">{{ SCArs.evolve("nūn") }}</span> &ldquo;now&rdquo; &nbsp;(Solar <i>nūn</i> — macron + tilde over one vowel)</li>
  <li><span class="heart big">{{ SCArs.evolve("ōn") }}</span> &ldquo;therefore&rdquo; &nbsp;(Solar <i>ōn</i>)</li>
  <li><span class="heart big">{{ SCArs.evolve("bendā") }}</span> &ldquo;chain&rdquo; &nbsp;(Solar <i>bendā</i>)</li>
  <li><span class="heart big">{{ SCArs.evolve("genton") }}</span> &ldquo;flesh&rdquo; &nbsp;(Solar <i>genton</i>)</li>
  <li><span class="heart big">{{ SCArs.evolve("kamtón") }}</span> &ldquo;hundred&rdquo; &nbsp;(Solar <i>kamtón</i>)</li>
  <li><span class="heart big">{{ SCArs.evolve("aiwon") }}</span> &ldquo;eternity&rdquo; &nbsp;(Solar <i>aiwon</i>)</li>
</ul>

<h2>A line of the Hymn to Wine</h2>
<p class="heart big">{{ Txt.cap(SCArs.evolve("zelā")) }}, {{ SCArs.evolve("dīwā") }}, {{ SCArs.evolve("sanā") }}.</p>
<p>&ldquo;Wine, heaven, song&rdquo; — Solar <i>zelā, dīwā, sanā</i>, evolved live by SCArs.</p>

<footer>Orpheus · Hymn server · Facet markup · SCArs sound-change applier on Loom.
&nbsp; Solar etyma from the Ligurian grammar; Heart forms computed, not stored.</footer>
